WEBVTT

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the World Champion, Dande…

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew…

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.310
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:37.030
This is Sakuragi Park, home to all the Pokémon
Satoshi and Go have caught.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.930
Another fun day at the Park
is about to begin!

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:49.070
Right…

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:52.070
Everyone! Good morning!

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.700
Good… Eat up!

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.710
Does that feel nice?

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.340
You guys bathe in the sand, huh?

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.120
There! All clean!

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.250
Now you, Rabbifoot!

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.210
Riolu! Vacuum Wave!

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:24.850
Barrierd! Reflector!

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.610
Riolu! Launch a flurry
of Vacuum Waves!

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.320
You can do it, Riolu!

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:40.610
Incoming call from Go.
Incoming call from Go.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:41.760
Yeah?

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:42.750
Satoshi!

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.520
You’re supposed to be helping
take care of the Pokémon in the Park!

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:46.540
Huh?

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.790
Oh, no! I forgot!

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.260
Sorry, Go!

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:53.250
I’m mostly done already.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.130
Really, I’m sorry.
What’s left that I can do?

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.380
Okay, you can brush
Hihidaruma’s teeth.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:00.390
Okay!

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:35.090
Hey! Hang on, you guys!

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.120
Quit fighting!

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.440
Something the matter?

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.580
Oh, you’ve already eaten?

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.210
You mean
you still want more?

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:49.940
What?
What are you angry about?

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.910
Stop! Stop!

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:01.510
What’s wrong?!

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:05.080
Huh? It’s empty already.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:06.910
Theirs, too?

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:09.790
Yeah. It was the same
everywhere I looked.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.340
They must have been
<i>really</i> hungry.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:14.130
I hope that’s all it is…

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.170
But the food’s been running out
really quick lately.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.920
It’s really strange.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:27.010
PocketMonsters

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.430
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.010
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.730
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.600
And skip the slow send-off

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.940
Be it through fire or through water

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.610
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:47.110
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:52.370
Each and every one of my memories

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:56.960
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.880
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:06.630
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:13.640
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:17.850
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.190
Let's have a fight!

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.900
1: Once the battle's done

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.730
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:28.070
On 3, let's be friends!

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.740
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:40.080
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.580
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:46.710
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:48.510
I choose you!

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:57.520
Sakuragi Park!
Massive Panic!

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:27.240
They’re being kinda aggressive.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:29.160
Something’s definitely weird here.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.410
We feed them plenty each day,

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:34.330
but maybe someone’s been hogging
all the Pokémon food to themselves?

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:36.790
And this someone ate <i>all</i> of it?

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.150
It might be a real glutton…

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:42.530
Or perhaps
just someone playing pranks?

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.100
Someone playing pranks?

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.760
What, Gänger?!

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:50.470
What?! Gänger?!

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.810
It really is fascinating,
I must say.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:06:59.800
Even in our small Sakuragi Park,

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:02.690
the Pokémon seem to have
formed communities.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:05.840
The Water-type Pokémon
gathered by the pond.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:08.550
The Pokémon huddled around Golugh.

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:13.200
Then there’s the prankster Muma
and the lone wolf Meguroco.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.950
One thing that concerns me, though,

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:17.900
is that the Bug-type Pokémon group,
the largest one,

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:21.080
seems to be
starting to clash with…

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.630
…the group consisting of
Normal types and Poison types.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.700
Now that you mention it,
I guess they do fight a lot.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:29.600
We have to solve the problem
of the food disappearing,

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:31.930
or the fighting will
just get worse.

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:36.600
Maybe some unknown Pokémon
snuck into the Park and is causing trouble?

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.140
Yeah, it could be.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:42.210
All right!
Let’s sleep over at the park tonight,

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:43.650
and stop the thief!

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:46.150
Okay!
We’ll catch them in the act, for sure!

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.150
We won’t let anyone suspicious
get away!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:15.650
Stay on your guard. It might be
some really violent glutton of a Pokémon!

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:25.040
Oh, just Nazonokusa?

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.960
They won’t be able to steal
<i>all</i> this food so easily.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.390
Let’s take turns keeping watch.

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:33.210
Sure!

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:46.920
Satoshi! It’s your turn.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.550
I’m counting on you.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:55.470
Sure! I got this!

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:02.490
Let’s catch the thief in the act
and brag about it to Go!

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:05.450
PocketMonsters

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.270
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:11.590
PocketMonsters

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:16.510
. Normal .
Hoshigarisu
PocketMonsters

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.520
Pikachu…
100,000 Volts…

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:35.860
What was that for, Pikachu?!

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:41.410
You’re kidding!

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.060
Satoshi.
Weren’t you keeping watch?

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:45.290
S-Sorry…

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:48.540
But did someone really
eat all of this on their own?

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:50.410
How much can they even eat?!

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.240
That’s…

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:12.630
Hey!

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:13.960
Hold it!

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:16.370
We gotta stop them,
Pikachu, Riolu!

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:17.570
Rabbifoot! Please!

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:31.070
It’s hopeless…
We can’t stop them!

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:34.110
Kairyu! Please, stop them!

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:38.210
H-Hey…

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:48.510
“Just watch”?

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:56.530
Is it saying to let the Pokémon in the Park
deal with their own problems?

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:57.830
Are you?

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:42.190
It’s Strike!

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:55.000
I really can’t leave them alone!

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.380
Hey! Wait!

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:13.760
Now even more are fighting!

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:15.000
L-Look!

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:19.540
It’s the Mayuld!

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.730
They look just about ready
to evolve!

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:31.990
Oh, no!

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:42.960
Golugh!

00:16:07.390 --> 00:16:10.060
Is this Golugh’s Rain Prayer?!

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:11.910
No, Rain Prayer couldn’t do <i>this!</i>

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:26.080
What? It’s acting strange!

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:28.180
What is going on, Rotom?!

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:33.310
It is said that removing the seal on Golugh’s chest
makes its internal energy go out of control.

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:35.990
We gotta stop Golugh!

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:36.800
Let’s go!

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:37.460
Yeah!

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:45.970
We just gotta seal its chest, right?

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:47.790
But how?

00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:54.490
You’ll all help?

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:57.420
All right!
We’ll draw Golugh’s attention away,

00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:59.160
and then you guys
replace the seal!

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:03.660
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:09.920
Rabbifoot! Ember!

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.640
Riolu! Fighting-type moves
won’t work on Golugh!

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:44.330
It’s back to normal!

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:46.950
But the rain isn’t stopping!

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:49.790
Mayuld!

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:52.800
Oh, no… They might not be able
to evolve like this!

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:25.750
Kairyu!

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:27.050
Let’s go, too!

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:28.080
Yeah! Of course!

00:18:28.510 --> 00:18:31.690
Dewgong! Menokurage!
Ice Beam!

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:11.760
Look! Everyone’s working together…

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:15.540
Yeah! All so the Mayuld can evolve!

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:44.990
They evolved…
into Dokucale…

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:48.660
It’s Dokucale’s Clear Skies.

00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:15.860
Figures they’d be hungry
after all that fighting.

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:20.030
They all worked together
to help Mayuld evolve…

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:22.540
Pokémon sure are complex creatures.

00:20:33.780 --> 00:20:36.320
Is this the disappeared
Pokémon food?!

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:54.180
H-Hoshigarisu…
You mean it was you?

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:56.180
Why would you…?

00:20:56.180 --> 00:20:59.420
Hang on. If I recall correctly,
Hoshigarisu was…

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:05.070
Hoshigarisu! Cheek-Stuffing Pokémon!
Normal type!

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:08.740
It’s prone to storing away food
in its hidden stash!

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:18.990
Guess we’d better start leaving food
for Hoshigarisu’s stash, too…

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:19.630
Yeah.

00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:29.100
And that was how
peace returned to Sakuragi Park.

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:40.610
The Pokémon’s paradise…

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:43.290
…is once again filled with
cheerful voices.

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:47.320
Let’s play Pokémon Shiritori!

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:48.530
